    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our clear offensive engine. Boasting an elite 87.14 score, he benefits from a perfect storm: the prime #2 spot in the order against a vulnerable Feltner, whose 4.96 xERA creates massive upside for a speed-based profile. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) are top-tier plays. **Mickey Moniak** leverages a significant +14% platoon edge against Kelly, while **Seiya Suzuki** feasts on a massive +19% SP skill bonus against Kent. Both provide high-floor production, helping us aggressively hunt for counting stats in an otherwise volatile mid-August environment.\n\nOur most difficult decision centered on **Austin Riley** (58.74) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (57.87). While **Tyler Soderstrom** sits on the cusp of being a \"Strong\" play, **Austin Riley** was squeezed into the UTIL spot despite a subpar #8 spot in the order. We are essentially betting on talent over the situational drag of the bottom-third of the lineup. Unfortunately, **Henry Bolte** (41.35) and **Max Muncy** (42.29) remain the most vulnerable starters in our lineup, largely hampered by the matchup against Rasmussen, whose 3.17 xERA suppresses their ceilings. With **James Wood**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested; we continue to monitor the status of **Jose Caballero**, **Trevor Story**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** to see if any late lineup shuffles or injury news necessitates a roster pivot. **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10) and **Isaac Paredes** (70.96) remain solid anchors, providing reliable output that allows us to absorb the risks currently attached to our lower-tier starters.",
